      "math_academy_id": "q-212938",
      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Given that $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7),$ construct a statement that also must be true:\n\n$$\na+{{field-1}}≡b+{{field-2}}\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The addition property of congruences states that\n\n$$\na≡b\\,⟺\\,a+c≡b+c\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can add the same integer to both sides of a congruence, keeping the modulus unchanged:\n\n$$\na≡b\\,⟺\\,a+1≡b+1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)\n$$",
